The "Print Matched Label" / waybill prompt used to save the PDF to the
desktop, forcing the packer to find and open the file before printing.
The prompt button now fetches the PDF and opens the browser's print
dialog straight from the preview via a hidden iframe (falls back to a
new tab if iframe printing is blocked). Nothing lands on the desktop.

Verified in Chromium: completing an order with a matched label shows
the prompt with a printer icon, and one click opens the print path
with no alerts or errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DuieZfw6EN7FaZSYKtjtbV
---
 public/app.js | 46 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/public/app.js b/public/app.js
index 468c8f1..ff07105 100644
